      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It's odd because this information is already stored, and any user can check who the instance master is in the world. But most don't as they don't know the keybind to pull up the networking debug menu or the steam launch option to enable this menu.\nSo I don't think this would be hard to implement but at the same time if anybody could see who the instance master is very easily then they could target them just to be an asshole, and if they wanted they could attempt to crash them to force another user to become the instance master. \nAnd not just that, even if they didn't want to fuck with the instance owner they would now easily know which user to avoid if they don't want to get kicked from the instance for say being toxic to other users or something like that.",
